Subject: Seasoned Cryomancer: do not refuse it over the stun step's unknown target count
Why: Before casting it the AI checks the whole ETB chain (draw two, discard two, then an
  immediate trigger that taps and stuns up to X creatures, X = nonland cards discarded). At that
  point X is 0, so TapAiBase.tapPrefTargeting finds no target, ImmediateTriggerAi.chkDrawback
  says no and the creature is refused (Dimir Uldaros, baseline: seen in 209 games, cast in 7).
  AILogic$ Always is the hint ImmediateTriggerAi already checks for; the stun targets are still
  chosen when the immediate trigger resolves, where the AI must pick them.
Measured: `mtgsim gauntlet decks/standard/meta/dimir-uldaros.txt --vs <the other ten meta decks> -n 100
  --seed 1`, default AI, Forge 7db198d72e, on 13 Nov 2026. Arm without patches: 30.1% (95% CI
  27-33%, 301-699). Arm with 0006 and 0007 together (separate shares not measured): 33.9%
  (31-37%, 339-661). Difference +3.8 points, 95% CI -0.3 to +7.9, p = 0.07: not a reliable
  change on 1,000 games each. Mirror on the patched engine (`match dimir-uldaros dimir-uldaros
  -n 200 --seed 1`): 51.0% (44-58%).
  Seasoned Cryomancer cast in 478 of 679 games where it was seen (13 of 695 without).

